searchData={"items":[{"type":"module","title":"Weaver","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.html"},{"type":"type","title":"Weaver.assistant_message/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.html#t:assistant_message/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Weaver.command/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.html#t:command/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Weaver.message/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.html#t:message/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Weaver.metric/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.html#t:metric/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Weaver.tool_call/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.html#t:tool_call/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Weaver.tool_message/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.html#t:tool_message/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Weaver.user_message/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.html#t:user_message/0"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Weaver.Api","doc":"`Weaver.Api` is a behaviour that describes an api `Weaver.LLM` can use","ref":"Weaver.Api.html"},{"type":"type","title":"Weaver.Api.response/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.Api.html#t:response/0"},{"type":"callback","title":"Weaver.Api.chat/1","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.Api.html#c:chat/1"},{"type":"callback","title":"Weaver.Api.start_link/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.Api.html#c:start_link/0"},{"type":"module","title":"Weaver.Api.Anthropic","doc":"Client for anthropic messages api. Built on https://anthropix.hexdocs.pm/Anthropix.html","ref":"Weaver.Api.Anthropic.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.Api.Anthropic.block_to_message/2","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.Api.Anthropic.html#block_to_message/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.Api.Anthropic.chat/1","doc":"Callback implementation for  Weaver.Api.chat/1 .","ref":"Weaver.Api.Anthropic.html#chat/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.Api.Anthropic.message_to_anthropic/1","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.Api.Anthropic.html#message_to_anthropic/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.Api.Anthropic.start_link/0","doc":"Callback implementation for  Weaver.Api.start_link/0 .","ref":"Weaver.Api.Anthropic.html#start_link/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.Api.Anthropic.translate_tool/1","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.Api.Anthropic.html#translate_tool/1"},{"type":"module","title":"Weaver.Api.Bedrock","doc":"Client for AWS Bedrock api. Built on https://ex-aws-bedrock.hexdocs.pm/ExAws.Bedrock.html","ref":"Weaver.Api.Bedrock.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.Api.Bedrock.chat/1","doc":"Callback implementation for  Weaver.Api.chat/1 .","ref":"Weaver.Api.Bedrock.html#chat/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.Api.Bedrock.parse_tool_calls/2","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.Api.Bedrock.html#parse_tool_calls/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.Api.Bedrock.start_link/0","doc":"Callback implementation for  Weaver.Api.start_link/0 .","ref":"Weaver.Api.Bedrock.html#start_link/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.Api.Bedrock.tool_call_parser/1","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.Api.Bedrock.html#tool_call_parser/1"},{"type":"module","title":"Weaver.Api.Bedrock.Request","doc":"`Weaver.Api.Bedrock.Request` handles converting sso credentials to something for ExAws and\nwraps ExAws.Bedrock.request to inject those creds when calling Bedrock.","ref":"Weaver.Api.Bedrock.Request.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.Api.Bedrock.Request.awscli_credential_process/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.Api.Bedrock.Request.html#awscli_credential_process/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.Api.Bedrock.Request.child_spec/1","doc":"Returns a specification to start this module under a supervisor.\n\nSee `Supervisor`.","ref":"Weaver.Api.Bedrock.Request.html#child_spec/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.Api.Bedrock.Request.request/2","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.Api.Bedrock.Request.html#request/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.Api.Bedrock.Request.start_link/1","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.Api.Bedrock.Request.html#start_link/1"},{"type":"module","title":"Weaver.Api.BedrockMock","doc":"Mock AWS Bedrock api","ref":"Weaver.Api.BedrockMock.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.Api.BedrockMock.chat/1","doc":"Callback implementation for  Weaver.Api.chat/1 .","ref":"Weaver.Api.BedrockMock.html#chat/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.Api.BedrockMock.start_link/0","doc":"Callback implementation for  Weaver.Api.start_link/0 .","ref":"Weaver.Api.BedrockMock.html#start_link/0"},{"type":"module","title":"Weaver.Api.Ollama","doc":"Ollama api client","ref":"Weaver.Api.Ollama.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Weaver.Api.OllamaMock","doc":"Mock Ollama api client","ref":"Weaver.Api.OllamaMock.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.Api.OllamaMock.chat/1","doc":"Callback implementation for  Weaver.Api.chat/1 .","ref":"Weaver.Api.OllamaMock.html#chat/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.Api.OllamaMock.start_link/0","doc":"Callback implementation for  Weaver.Api.start_link/0 .","ref":"Weaver.Api.OllamaMock.html#start_link/0"},{"type":"module","title":"Weaver.Api.OpenAI","doc":"Client for OpenAI apis","ref":"Weaver.Api.OpenAI.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Weaver.Application","doc":"The entrypoint for the application","ref":"Weaver.Application.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Weaver.CLI","doc":"`Weaver.CLI` handles displaying messages to the user in the terminal.\n\nIt subscribes to the `\"messages\"` Phoenix.PubSub topic and renders conversation\nmessages with appropriate formatting. Thinking content is shown in cyan, chat\nresponses are displayed using Marcli for markdown formatting, and tool calls\nare listed in yellow. The module handles user prompts and recognizes slash\ncommands for quitting or other special operations.","ref":"Weaver.CLI.html"},{"type":"type","title":"Weaver.CLI.t/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.html#t:t/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.child_spec/1","doc":"Returns a specification to start this module under a supervisor.\n\nSee `Supervisor`.","ref":"Weaver.CLI.html#child_spec/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.start_link/1","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.html#start_link/1"},{"type":"module","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI","doc":"ANSI control sequences not provided by IO.ANSI","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html"},{"type":"module","title":"References - Weaver.CLI.ANSI","doc":"https://invisible-island.net/xterm/ctlseqs/ctlseqs.html\nhttps://gist.github.com/fnky/458719343aabd01cfb17a3a4f7296797","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html#module-references"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.cursor_backward/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html#cursor_backward/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.cursor_backward/1","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html#cursor_backward/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.cursor_column/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html#cursor_column/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.cursor_column/1","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html#cursor_column/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.cursor_down/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html#cursor_down/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.cursor_down/1","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html#cursor_down/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.cursor_forward/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html#cursor_forward/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.cursor_forward/1","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html#cursor_forward/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.cursor_next_line/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html#cursor_next_line/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.cursor_next_line/1","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html#cursor_next_line/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.cursor_position/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html#cursor_position/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.cursor_position/1","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html#cursor_position/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.cursor_preceding_line/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html#cursor_preceding_line/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.cursor_preceding_line/1","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html#cursor_preceding_line/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.cursor_up/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html#cursor_up/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.cursor_up/1","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html#cursor_up/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.delete_characters/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html#delete_characters/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.delete_characters/1","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html#delete_characters/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.delete_lines/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html#delete_lines/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.delete_lines/1","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html#delete_lines/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.display_erase_above/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html#display_erase_above/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.display_erase_all/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html#display_erase_all/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.display_erase_below/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html#display_erase_below/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.format/1","doc":"Use `format/1` like [`IO.ANSI.format/2`](https://elixir.hexdocs.pm/1.20.4/IO.ANSI.html#format/2). Calls\nIO.ANSI so all escapes supported there can be used here.\n\n```elixir\n[:display_erase_all, {:cursor_position, {10, 10}}, :red, \"Hello world!\"]\n|> Weaver.CLI.ANSI.format()\n|> IO.puts()\n```","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html#format/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.insert_blank/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html#insert_blank/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.insert_blank/1","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html#insert_blank/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.insert_lines/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html#insert_lines/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.insert_lines/1","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html#insert_lines/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.line_erase_all/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html#line_erase_all/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.line_erase_left/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html#line_erase_left/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.line_erase_right/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html#line_erase_right/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.shift_left/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html#shift_left/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.shift_left/1","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html#shift_left/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.shift_right/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html#shift_right/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.shift_right/1","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.html#shift_right/1"},{"type":"module","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.Macros","doc":"Helpers to reduce boilerplate for handling ANSI control sequences","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.Macros.html"},{"type":"macro","title":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.Macros.build_commands/1","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.ANSI.Macros.html#build_commands/1"},{"type":"module","title":"Weaver.CLI.IO","doc":"Allows the user prompt to be handled async. Relies on `Weaver.CLI.Term` for configuring the terminal.\n\nThe standard `IO` moudle should not be used when using `Weaver.CLI.IO`. In order for this module to\nkeep the prompt at the bottom of the display no other process can write to stdout.","ref":"Weaver.CLI.IO.html"},{"type":"type","title":"Weaver.CLI.IO.t/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.IO.html#t:t/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Weaver.CLI.IO.term_config/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.IO.html#t:term_config/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.IO.child_spec/1","doc":"Returns a specification to start this module under a supervisor.\n\nSee `Supervisor`.","ref":"Weaver.CLI.IO.html#child_spec/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.IO.prompt/1","doc":"Display a prompt collecting keyboard input until enter is pressed.\n\nOnce the user presses enter a message will be sent to the caller like\n```elixir\n{:keyboard_input, String.t()}\n```\nand polling will be stopped.","ref":"Weaver.CLI.IO.html#prompt/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.IO.puts/1","doc":"Write to stdout like IO.puts/2.\n\nThis will interrupt any prompt (if it is collecting input) so that output can be displayed\nthen the prompt will be displayed again after the output.","ref":"Weaver.CLI.IO.html#puts/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.IO.start_link/1","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.IO.html#start_link/1"},{"type":"module","title":"Weaver.CLI.SlashCommands","doc":"Helpers for `Weaver.CLI` slash commands like /exit, /clear, etc.","ref":"Weaver.CLI.SlashCommands.html"},{"type":"macro","title":"Weaver.CLI.SlashCommands.generate_slash_commands/1","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.CLI.SlashCommands.html#generate_slash_commands/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.CLI.SlashCommands.help/1","doc":"Displays all the slash commands and their help strings","ref":"Weaver.CLI.SlashCommands.html#help/1"},{"type":"module","title":"Weaver.History","doc":"Persists conversation messages to JSONL files.\n\nSubscribes to the `\"messages\"` and `\"commands\"` Phoenix.PubSub topics,\nencoding each message/command as JSON and appending to timestamped files.\nEach new conversation or resume creates a new file with an ISO 8601 timestamp.\nThe file descriptor is properly closed when the server terminates.","ref":"Weaver.History.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Config - Weaver.History","doc":"| Key | Description |\n|-----|-------------|\n| `:base_dir` | The directory where history files are stored (default: `.weaver/history/`) |","ref":"Weaver.History.html#module-config"},{"type":"module","title":"History Resumption - Weaver.History","doc":"Use `resume/1` to replay messages from a previous session file. This broadcasts\nall messages back to the `\"messages\"` topic and commands to the `\"commands\"` topic,\nallowing other components to reconstruct their state.","ref":"Weaver.History.html#module-history-resumption"},{"type":"type","title":"Weaver.History.config/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.History.html#t:config/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Weaver.History.file_descriptor/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.History.html#t:file_descriptor/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Weaver.History.formatted_command/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.History.html#t:formatted_command/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Weaver.History.pubsub_name/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.History.html#t:pubsub_name/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Weaver.History.state/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.History.html#t:state/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.History.child_spec/1","doc":"Returns a specification to start this module under a supervisor.\n\nSee `Supervisor`.","ref":"Weaver.History.html#child_spec/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.History.resume/1","doc":"Resumes a previous conversation by replaying messages from the given history file.\n\nBroadcasts all messages to the `\"messages\"` topic and commands to the `\"commands\"` topic\nwith a `resume: true` flag. After completion, broadcasts `:resume_end` and initializes\na new history file for the resumed conversation.","ref":"Weaver.History.html#resume/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.History.resume/2","doc":"Resumes a previous conversation by replaying messages from the given history file\non the specified process.","ref":"Weaver.History.html#resume/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.History.sessions/0","doc":"Lists all available history sessions (JSONL files).\n\nReturns a sorted list of history file names.","ref":"Weaver.History.html#sessions/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.History.sessions/1","doc":"Lists all available history sessions (JSONL files) from the specified process.","ref":"Weaver.History.html#sessions/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.History.start_link/1","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.History.html#start_link/1"},{"type":"module","title":"Weaver.LLM","doc":"Maintains conversation context and manages LLM interactions.\n\n`Weaver.LLM` ties together the API and messages topic by:\n- Maintaining conversation context with system prompt and message history\n- Calling the API for each LLM turn\n- Broadcasting responses to all subscribers","ref":"Weaver.LLM.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Configuration - Weaver.LLM","doc":"config :weaver,\n      llm: [api: Elixir.Module.That.Implements.Weaver.Api]\n\n| Key | Description |\n|-----|------|\n| `:api` | An elixir module that implements the `Weaver.Api` behaviour |","ref":"Weaver.LLM.html#module-configuration"},{"type":"type","title":"Weaver.LLM.context/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.LLM.html#t:context/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Weaver.LLM.t/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.LLM.html#t:t/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.LLM.child_spec/1","doc":"Returns a specification to start this module under a supervisor.\n\nSee `Supervisor`.","ref":"Weaver.LLM.html#child_spec/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.LLM.start_link/1","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.LLM.html#start_link/1"},{"type":"module","title":"Weaver.Personas","doc":"`Weaver.Personas` handles loading persona details from persona.json and PERSONA.md files.\n\nA persona is built from a `persona.json` and a `PERSONA.md` in a directory named for the persona.\n\n#### `persona.json`\n\n```json\n{\n  \"model\": \"model-name-or-id\",\n  \"api\": \"Api.Module.Name\",\n  \"context_window\": 128000,\n  \"output_tokens\": 16000,\n  \"temperature\": 0.6,\n  \"top_p\": 0.95,\n  \"top_k\": 20,\n  \"tools\": [\n    \"list\",\n    \"of\",\n    \"tools\",\n    \"model\",\n    \"can\",\n    \"use\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n| Key | Description |\n|-----|-------------|\n| `\"model\"` | The name or id of the model in a format that the api client can use |\n| `\"api\"` | The elixir module to use as the api backend that implements the `Weaver.Api` behaviour |\n| `\"context_window\"` | The maximum number of tokens the context is allowed to use |\n| `\"output_tokens\"` | The maximum number of output tokens to generate |\n| `\"temperature\"` | Temperature value to pass to the model |\n| `\"top_p\"` | Top p value to pass to the model |\n| `\"top_k\"` | Top k value to pass to the model |\n| `\"tools\"` | A list of tool names this persona is allowed to call |\n\n#### `PERSONA.md`\n\nThe `PERSONA.md` file is used as the system prompt. It can be empty.\n\n#### Config\n\n| Key | Description |\n|-----|-------------|\n| `:base_dir` | The base directory to search for personas |\n| `:name` | The name of the persona must match its dirname in the personas base dir |","ref":"Weaver.Personas.html"},{"type":"type","title":"Weaver.Personas.model_options/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.Personas.html#t:model_options/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Weaver.Personas.t/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.Personas.html#t:t/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.Personas.model/1","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.Personas.html#model/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.Personas.model_options/1","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.Personas.html#model_options/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.Personas.system_prompt/1","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.Personas.html#system_prompt/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.Personas.tools_available/1","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.Personas.html#tools_available/1"},{"type":"module","title":"Weaver.Tools","doc":"Manages tool execution and responses.\n\n`Weaver.Tools` handles calling tools via a STDIO interface or by invoking Elixir modules\nthat implement the `Weaver.Tools.Tool` behaviour. It broadcasts a list of tool response\nmessages to the `\"messages\"` topic, or broadcasts to `\"commands\"` if a terminal tool\ncall is encountered.\n\n#### STDIO Interface\n\nA STDIO tool requires:\n- A `definition.json` file in the tool's directory\n- A `run` executable/script that accepts JSON input via STDIN\n- Output to STDIO is sent to the llm verbatim\n- The tool's path will be built like ` / /`\n\n#### Behaviour\n\nAn elixir tool must implement the `Weaver.Tool` behaviour.\n\n#### Config\n\n| Key | Description |\n|-----|-------------|\n| `:base_dir` | The directory containing STDIO tools |\n| `:tool_modules` | A map of tool names to elixir modules |","ref":"Weaver.Tools.html"},{"type":"type","title":"Weaver.Tools.definition/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.Tools.html#t:definition/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Weaver.Tools.json_schema/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.Tools.html#t:json_schema/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Weaver.Tools.t/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.Tools.html#t:t/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.Tools.child_spec/1","doc":"Returns a specification to start this module under a supervisor.\n\nSee `Supervisor`.","ref":"Weaver.Tools.html#child_spec/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.Tools.get_tool_definitions/1","doc":"Retrieves the definitions for the given list of tools.\n\nReturns a list of tool definition maps. If a tool is registered as an Elixir\nmodule, its `c:Weaver.Tools.Tool.definition/0` callback is invoked. Otherwise,\nthe definition is loaded from the tool's `definition.json` file via the STDIO interface.","ref":"Weaver.Tools.html#get_tool_definitions/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Weaver.Tools.start_link/1","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.Tools.html#start_link/1"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Weaver.Tools.Tool","doc":"A behaviour for implementing tools as elixir modules","ref":"Weaver.Tools.Tool.html"},{"type":"callback","title":"Weaver.Tools.Tool.definition/0","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.Tools.Tool.html#c:definition/0"},{"type":"callback","title":"Weaver.Tools.Tool.run/1","doc":"","ref":"Weaver.Tools.Tool.html#c:run/1"},{"type":"extras","title":"Weaver","doc":"# Weaver\n\nAgent framework and cli.","ref":"readme.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"CLI - Weaver","doc":"Run `./weaver` after setting the config options to use `weaver` as an interactive cli tool.","ref":"readme.html#cli"},{"type":"extras","title":"Config - Weaver","doc":"Api modules may require additional configuration.\n\n| ENV Var | Description | Default |\n|---|---|---|\n| `WEAVER_PERSONA` | The [persona](#personas) to use with `weaver`. | |\n| `WEAVER_PERSONAS_BASE_DIR` | The directory that has personas. | |\n| `WEAVER_TOOLS_BASE_DIR` | The directory that has `STDIO` [tools](#tools). | |\n| `WEAVER_HISTORY_BASE_DIR` | The directory for `Weaver.History` to output jsonl files. | `.weaver/history` |\n| `WEAVER_SHOW_THINKING` | Show thinking output in the TUI or not. | `\"yes\"` |","ref":"readme.html#config"},{"type":"extras","title":"Framework - Weaver","doc":"As a framework `weaver`'s goal is to be very flexible. To achieve that all core communication happens over `Phoenix.PubSub` so that process can choose what to consume and how to deal with the messages.\n\n### `Phoenix.PubSub`\n\nThere are three topics that a process can subscribe to: \n\n* `\"messages\"`\n  * Where each message in the agent's conversation is broadcast.\n* `\"commands\"`\n  * Where commands (like `:clear` and `:compact`) are broadcast.\n* `\"metrics\"`\n  * Where token usage metrics are broadcast.\n  \nThe types for each are on `Weaver`.","ref":"readme.html#framework"},{"type":"extras","title":"Processes - Weaver","doc":"The processes that `weaver` starts can be configured like\n\n```elixir\nconfig :weaver,\n  processes: [\n    DynamicSupervisor,\n    Phoenix.PubSub,\n    Weaver.History,\n    Weaver.Tools,\n    Weaver.LLM,\n    Weaver.CLI\n  ]\n```\n\nOmitting a process from this list will prevent it from starting so that you can start another process instead (or none at all). See `config/test.exs` for an example. See `Weaver.Application` for a complete list of processes.","ref":"readme.html#processes"},{"type":"extras","title":"Tools - Weaver","doc":"Tools can be implemented against the `STDIO` interface or as Elixir modules. Some `STDIO` tools can be found in `tools/`. See `Weaver.Tools` for more details.","ref":"readme.html#tools"},{"type":"extras","title":"Personas - Weaver","doc":"A persona is a directory with `PERSONA.md` and `persona.json` files that describe it. Some default personas can be found in `personas/`. See `Weaver.Personas` for more details.\n\n```text\n${WEAVER_PERSONAS_BASE_DIR}/\n├──  \n│   ├── persona.json\n│   ├── PERSONA.md\n└──  \n    ├── persona.json\n    └── PERSONA.md\n```","ref":"readme.html#personas"}],"proglang":"elixir","content_type":"text/markdown","producer":{"name":"ex_doc","version":"0.40.4"}}